From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000005 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReForge <reforge@flashforge>
Date: Fri, 05 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mcu: relax TRSYNC_TIMEOUT for AD5M (preempts E0011)

The AD5M/Pro carries two Nationstech N32G455 MCUs (mainboard +
toolhead) speaking Klipper-11 protocol over UART at 230400.  Multiple
forge-x users have reported sporadic E0011 ("MCU communication
timeout") shutdowns mid-print on this hardware, traced to the host's
trsync acknowledgement deadline expiring before the toolhead MCU can
reply across the shared bus.

Doubling TRSYNC_TIMEOUT from 25 ms to 50 ms gives the MCU enough
headroom without measurably affecting responsiveness -- trsync
deadlines guard stepper-sync correctness, not user-facing latency.
forge-x has shipped this same value in
.shell/commands/ztune_klipper.sh's fix_enable_e11 for years across
the AD5M user base without regressions.

We carry it as a preemptive default (2026-06-05) instead of waiting
for an E0011 to be observed on our specific test unit -- the
hardware class is identical and the field evidence is strong enough.
If we ever do hit a hard-to-diagnose problem that traces back to a
longer trsync window, this single patch reverts it.

Upstream Klipper master still ships 0.025; no PR thread to back-link.

Signed-off-by: ReForge <reforge@flashforge>
---
 klippy/mcu.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/klippy/mcu.py b/klippy/mcu.py
--- a/klippy/mcu.py
+++ b/klippy/mcu.py
@@ -125,7 +125,7 @@
             s.note_homing_end()
         return params['trigger_reason']
 
-TRSYNC_TIMEOUT = 0.025
+TRSYNC_TIMEOUT = 0.05
 TRSYNC_SINGLE_MCU_TIMEOUT = 0.250
 
 class MCU_endstop:
-- 
2.47.0
